PART H — CALCULATION RULES (one shared function, used everywhere)
================
H1. Duration: Out − In. If Out is earlier than In, treat it as next-day (overnight) and add 24h. Open records ("Working Now", no Out) show "—" for hours and are excluded from totals until closed, except Dashboard "hours so far" which counts to now.
H2. Rounding applies to the punch times first (separately for In and Out, using Company Settings), then duration is computed.
H3. Lunch: (a) if the record has explicit Lunch Start/End (sheet entry), deduct that duration; (b) else if Auto Lunch Deduction applies (company setting, or the user's per-user setting), deduct the configured Minutes once the worked duration reaches the After X Hours threshold. Never deduct twice.
H4. Totals: Paid = Reg + OT + paid Absence hours + Hours-type Adjustments (Addition +, Deduction −). Unpaid = unpaid Absence hours. Total = Paid + Unpaid. All displays use the company's Time Totals Format setting.
H5. Pay Period for a company is anchored on its Pay Period Start Date and repeats by its Pay Period type; "This Pay Period" quick filters and the Dashboard use it. The landing sheet keeps its own independent Period Starting behavior.
H6. Late IN = In later than Default Shift Start + 5 minutes. Early OUT = Out earlier than Default Shift End. These flags show as small tags in List View and drive notifications.
